														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2701236">
									

<p>I like this, but are the footnotes describing what adipocytes, organelles, and endoplasmic reticulum are really necessary? I understand that not everyone who reads them understand what they mean, but it ruins the immersion a little bit, because I imagine the people who work at the Foundation are pretty smart, and know what they are.</p>
<p>Also, just another little biology term, you said that endoplasmic reticulums synthesise lipids; you're partially right, if you want to be more technical, say that it's the smooth endoplasmic reticulum, which is the one that synthesises lipids. The other one, the rough endoplasmic reticulum, is responsible for the synthesis of proteins (via attached ribosomes), and packaging of said proteins.</p>
<p>Other than that, very good first SCP, take my upvote :)</p>

